# libFuzzer dictionary for auth_headers_fuzzer (auth.verify_proxy_hmac +
# auth.parse_bearer). Both parsers are gated on literal tokens — the `t=`/`v1=`
# key names of the X-Proxy-Auth header and the `Bearer` scheme — that Atheris'
# random FuzzedDataProvider bytes essentially never synthesise, so without this
# dict the harness only ever exercises the "no key found" reject path.
# Non-ASCII entries use \xNN escapes (libFuzzer dict format). See fuzz/README.md.
"t="
"v1="
","
"="
"t=1700000000"
"t=1700000000,v1="
"v1=0123456789abcdef"
# `int(t_raw)` accepts far more than plain ASCII digits — a sign, underscores, an
# over-long literal and non-ASCII digits each reach a different branch.
"+1700000000"
"-1700000000"
"1_700_000_000"
# Arabic-Indic digits U+0661..0663 (int() accepts them; the HMAC then must not).
"\xd9\xa1\xd9\xa2\xd9\xa3"
# A non-ASCII signature byte — the isascii() guard that replaced a compare_digest
# TypeError.
"v1=\xc3\xbf"
# Authorization: Bearer <token>
"Bearer "
"bearer "
"BEARER "
"Bearer clauster_pat_"
